<Page title="about · almo7aya.dev" window="TYPE ABOUT.TXT">
  <h1>Ali Almo<span class="s7">7</span>aya</h1>
  <p class="meta">Staff Web Engineer @ Anghami &amp; OSN+ · Yemen → Riyadh · <a href="https://github.com/Almo7aya">github.com/Almo7aya</a></p>
  <p>I'm a Staff Web Engineer at Anghami and OSN+, where I build the web and smart-TV apps for both streaming services. I specialise in video playback and DRM: getting protected content to start fast and play smoothly on every browser and TV it ships to. It's my favourite kind of work: when it's done right, nobody notices, they just watch.</p>
  <p><b>Skills:</b> TypeScript, JavaScript, React, Preact, Node.js, C++, Go, Rust, Lua, Docker, GitHub Actions, Linux and OpenWrt.</p>
  <p>Beyond the web I like it close to the metal: low-level programming, emulation, C++ and graphics, for the simple joy of watching something boot. I also maintain <a href="https://github.com/Almo7aya/openingh.nvim">openingh.nvim</a> and <a href="https://github.com/Almo7aya/neogruvbox.nvim">neogruvbox.nvim</a> for Neovim and <a href="https://github.com/Almo7aya/luci-app-gowan">GoWAN</a> for OpenWrt, and I've had patches merged in Preact, LunarVim and nvim-tree. The home page of this site is an 8086 PC emulator I wrote, booting operating systems, games and demos I also wrote, which is what happens when a web engineer is left alone with an assembler.</p>
